// github_merge_queue.proto — A GITHUB MERGE QUEUE AS THE DAEMON FOLLOWS IT
// for a workspace: which queue, the subscription that follows it, what the
// queue holds now, and each change the daemon tells the subscriber about.
// Shared by the merge-queue endpoints (SubscribeGithubMergeQueue,
// UnsubscribeGithubMergeQueue, ListGithubMergeQueueSubscriptions) and by the
// notice the daemon delivers (GithubMergeQueueNotice).
//
// THIS IS GITHUB'S MERGE QUEUE, the queue a repository's branch protection
// runs on github.com, and nothing of agent-repl's own landing queue
// (merge_queue_status.proto, SubscribeMergeQueue), which shares only the
// words.
//
// FOLLOWING ONE PULL REQUEST through its queue needs none of this: it is the
// pull-request subscription's PULL_REQUEST_NOTICE_EVENT_MERGE_QUEUE event
// (pull_request.proto). This file is for a workspace that watches a whole
// queue move, whoever's pull requests are in it.
//
// THE DAEMON READS, THE AGENT IS TOLD, as for a pull request. The daemon
// reads the queue's entries in order on its pull-request cadence, compares
// them with what it last told each subscriber, and tells only the
// difference. An entry that left is read once more, to tell whether it
// merged or was removed, and why. A read missed while the daemon was down is
// made up by the next one, which compares against what was last told: an
// entry can be told late, never lost. An entry that joined and left between
// two reads is never seen by this subscription, which follows the queue's
// standing order; following one pull request (the event above) reads its
// timeline instead and misses no joining.
//
// TOLD ONCE. What a subscriber was told is recorded with the subscription in
// the same transaction as its notice, as for a pull request.

